WEBVTT

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:15.770
Excuse me, Segawa-sensei, what's the matter?

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.140
Oh, my... Amagasa-sensei.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:22.410
Ah, pardon me, I didn't mean...

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:25.240
This morning my little Yuuki came down with a fever.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:24.740
Ignored

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:29.420
I made rice porridge for breakfast, and put the leftovers in the refrigerator, saying:

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:32.690
"If you think you can eat it, do so."

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.340
But that's no good, is it?

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.880
So you have a little one?

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.190
I'm just going to go check on her!

00:02:42.190 --> 00:02:47.860
Amagasa-sensei, I have your homeroom class next, so...

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.480
I don't mind, I'm free.

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:52.790
It's okay?!

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:56.860
Y-Y-You are welcome?  Is that right?

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.070
Berry guddo desu!

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.940
Did Segawa-sensei have a child?

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:16.090
Roger.  This three-man cell is on patrol.  Over.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.030
What?

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:17.960
Scheduled check-in.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.210
Yo.

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:28.750
Art begins from self-expression and ends in self-expression.

00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.020
Natsume Souseki said something like that.

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.520
What was he saying?

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.240
Ushio, look here!

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.600
That picture from before...

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:42.450
Oh that?

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.770
In the end...

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:44.660
...the arm didn't fly off.

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.820
That is not correct!

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:57.500
Torako-san, look, look!  No, look at that!

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:03.320
Damn it, I lost!

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:05.430
It's cause you're blabbing my ear off, Ta-chan!

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:09.090
Or rather your pitiful skills are the ones...

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:07.640
The teacher is coming.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.480
Yo!

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:13.760
Oh, Sensei.  We have English next, you know.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.580
Not anymore.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.690
Suzume-san, did you just...

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.610
Listen up, everyone.

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:23.010
The English teacher, Segawa-sensei, had some stuff come up suddenly,

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:25.190
so this period is free-study.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.120
Everyone do a...

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:30.410
Oh, you have gym next?

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:33.710
In that case, everyone get changed and get some exercise in the gym.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.520
Yippee!

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.120
What?

00:04:46.150 --> 00:04:48.090
Understood.  We'll head right over.

00:04:48.090 --> 00:04:49.770
Great job on the info.

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:54.080
I'm gonna sketch over in the gym.

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:54.920
What about you guys?

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.020
I'll go too.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.320
Me, too, then.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.020
Then off we go.

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.960
We're currently in Gym #2, the new one.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.160
Don't get it wrong, okay?

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:13.980
Roger.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:17.530
You're sure rarin' to go.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.710
It's important to stretch beforehand.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:24.320
The new gym really is quite nice.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.570
And it's number 2!  Number 2!

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:27.850
So, what?

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:30.930
Um, it's just such a big school, see, and...

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.890
This sucks...

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.400
It's free-study, so we don't actually have to do anything, right?

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.130
Yeah.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:43.760
But we went and changed and everything...

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:46.870
And the teacher came too.

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.820
This ain't no self-study...

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:51.660
Oh, you're right!

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:01.830
Hey!

00:06:01.830 --> 00:06:03.280
Crap, we're found out!

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:04.080
What'll we do?

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.260
Don't panic.

00:06:05.580 --> 00:06:06.970
What are you doing?

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:08.960
Expressing ourselves.

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.150
Note:  Bunten (1910's Japanese art exhibition) and the Creative Arts (written 1912)

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:12.150
Natsume Souseki's "Bunten to Geijutsu," right?

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.430
Seems you know a thing or two.

00:06:13.730 --> 00:06:16.420
We're in the land of our favorite subjects.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.440
Maybe I should keep a hold of that camera.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:27.600
Well then, we'd better decide what to draw, or...

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.620
That's, Torako-chan!

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:31.230
That's, Torako!

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:34.570
So that's Torako's class?

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:35.990
Should I yell out to her?

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:39.040
Naw, I'll check her out quietly and tease her later.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.320
This was Torako-chan's class?

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:43.290
So cute!

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.880
So cute, it must be a violation of the rules!

00:06:46.180 --> 00:06:47.760
Let's do it.

00:06:48.060 --> 00:06:51.550
Hmm, what should we do?

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:56.220
Basketball?  Volleyball?

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:59.270
Badminton?  Maybe table tennis?

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.070
What should we do?

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.430
What is she doing?

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:21.010
So, what'll it be?

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:22.050
What will what be?

00:07:22.050 --> 00:07:24.420
Don't ask me!

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:26.930
Hey, you guys, participate!

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.930
But I'm no good at sports.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.420
What she said.

00:07:32.420 --> 00:07:33.850
Me too.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:36.950
You just don't wanna do it!

00:07:36.950 --> 00:07:38.820
Cause it's boring!

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.470
Whatever!  All of you are in!

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:42.810
You too, Ayu!

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:54.470
And you, Touma!

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.330
They still haven't started yet?

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.250
You know... Girls...

00:08:09.410 --> 00:08:13.140
I guess it's impossible to take it back from down there without him noticing.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:14.040
Damn it.

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.570
And yet, there they are, my golden nest eggs, just hanging about lazily before me!

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:23.320
And what's more, they are dressed in their gym uniforms and it's not the sports festival!

00:08:23.320 --> 00:08:27.170
Unless it's a baseball tournament or a sports festival,

00:08:27.170 --> 00:08:30.620
someone in a different school year like me has no other chance for this rare shot!

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:35.860
I've got no other choice.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:40.040
The resolution is poor, so I wish I didn't have to use it,

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.830
but a man's gotta do what a man's gotta do!

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:49.400
Tiny hidden camera with wireless bluetooth connectivity!

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.450
Oops, said that aloud.

00:08:50.800 --> 00:09:02.060
Oh, Torako-chan... You're just so cute!

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:53.160
How much was that?

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.490
Retails for 398.

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.070
Whoa, pricey!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.610
It's quite a bargain when you think of the specs.

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:01.150
Shall we begin?

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.060
That's the camera?

00:09:02.360 --> 00:09:04.180
So, palms up or down, right?

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:06.320
Huh, what?

00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:08.190
It's a way to split up the teams.

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:10.890
What's that?  Not rock and paper?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:12.400
It's rock and paper for me.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:17.360
Palms up or down... Palms up or down!

00:09:17.360 --> 00:09:19.230
It's rock paper, jyan!  (jyan = isn't it)

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:23.370
I've always done rock paper, jyas!

00:09:19.230 --> 00:09:23.370
Jyas

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.220
What the heck is "jyas"?

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.830
"Jya?"  What's the "?"

00:09:25.220 --> 00:09:26.830
Whatever.

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:30.040
How about using the color of the underwear you're wearing today.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:33.380
I'm the black team.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:34.340
Nakai-chan

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:34.340
Miura-san

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:34.340
The white team!

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.300
Sakai-san

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.300
Yui-san

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:35.300
Shinohara-san

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:35.300
The beige team!

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.260
Makimura-san

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.260
Morioka-san

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:36.260
Yoshizaki-san

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:36.260
The checkered team!

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:37.470
The polka dot team!

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:40.030
What the heck kind of teams are you making?

00:09:40.030 --> 00:09:41.420
Which team might you two be?!

00:09:41.420 --> 00:09:42.580
Stop it!

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:52.870
You just want to look at them, you damn pervert!

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.000
Fine, then today...

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.610
No more speaking, Nene House!

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:58.610
Under Arrest

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.670
So, what were we talking about?

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:02.130
We were splitting up into teams!

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:03.350
Oh, right.

00:10:03.350 --> 00:10:04.830
Let's just do it simply.

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.660
Did you eat rice or bread for breakfast?

00:10:07.660 --> 00:10:09.500
Who cares about that?

00:10:09.800 --> 00:10:12.250
I had rice, and natto, and...

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:12.820
...Nori?

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:13.970
Don't go encouraging her!

00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:15.850
But I didn't think you'd be so Japanese.

00:10:15.850 --> 00:10:16.960
Bread.

00:10:21.470 --> 00:10:24.010
Things seem to have gotten off track.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.600
Yeah... Girls...

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:30.930
Yanagi...

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:31.750
What?

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:33.190
Are you hungry or something?

00:10:33.190 --> 00:10:34.390
No!

00:10:34.390 --> 00:10:35.980
You're like some begging monk.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:37.260
Leave me alone!

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:40.610
Hey!  In that case, make a bread team and a rice team!

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:43.350
Split us up like that?

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.870
Wait, Sensei-

00:10:45.530 --> 00:10:47.630
It is free-study.

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:48.380
Yes!

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.580
Then who's gonna supervise?

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:52.390
Well, this is just perfect.

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:54.130
Teach, did you bring a whistle?

00:10:55.140 --> 00:10:56.000
That's exactly...

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.130
...what I planned all along!

00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:02.090
Awesome!

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:05.850
Makenouchi-kun, I think I might be on the road to recovery, so...

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:04.640
What's he so excited about?

00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:06.970
I don't get it...

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:06.970
Makenouchi-kun?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.020
And so

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:15.980
Rice Team

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.950
So, what else did you have?

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.120
Fried egg, sunny-side up.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:20.680
As did I.

00:11:20.680 --> 00:11:21.930
Natto and nori!

00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:23.010
Me, too!

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.000
A slice of grilled salmon seasoned with salt.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:25.990
Same for me.

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:26.950
Bread Team

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:28.780
So did you have white bread?

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:30.900
Yes, white bread.

00:11:30.900 --> 00:11:32.720
Strawberry jam.

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:35.030
You got a problem with strawberry jam?

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:37.460
That's nice... Strawberry jam...

00:11:37.500 --> 00:11:39.670
Don't look at me with those eyes!

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:40.340
Scorekeeper

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:44.490
Kazamatsuri-san?

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:47.830
What else can I do?  I skipped breakfast.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.180
I'm already about to pass out.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.310
You shouldn't do that!

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.610
Female high school kids shouldn't...

00:11:51.870 --> 00:11:54.110
Man, I'm hungry.

00:11:54.110 --> 00:11:57.060
So... What are we doing exactly?

00:11:57.340 --> 00:12:01.030
Um...  Dodgeball he said...

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:02.990
Dodgeball?

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.030
Nice.

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:05.230
Not bad, eh?

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:06.560
"Dodge?"

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:07.970
Torako-san, I am waiting.

00:12:07.970 --> 00:12:08.780
For?

00:12:08.780 --> 00:12:12.200
You know, for you to name everyone with famous player's names...

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:14.340
I'm not gonna do that.

00:12:14.340 --> 00:12:16.520
Maybe you have matured a little...

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:19.820
'cause I don't know any famous dodgeball players.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:21.910
Then how about original names!

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.220
Original?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:24.970
Dragon Princess!

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:27.780
Note:  All the names Torako creates are the literal meanings of the kanji in the character's first names.

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:27.560
Dragon Princess?

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:29.930
Something like this?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:34.430
What about me?  What about me?

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:34.430
I just translated your name into English, Ta-chan.

00:12:34.430 --> 00:12:35.310
What about me?

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:36.400
Tiger Kid!

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.170
What about me?  What about me?

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:43.230
I can't wait, I can't wait, I can't wait!

00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:45.370
Minato is...

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:51.990
What is "minato" in English?

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:52.920
Harbor!

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:54.750
Then, Harbor Bunny!

00:12:57.670 --> 00:13:00.090
Amusement Palace

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:04.510
What is it?

00:13:05.120 --> 00:13:07.110
Walking...

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:14.390
Uh... I don't really know!

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:17.020
I'll ask my father for the next time.

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:17.900
Nonomura-kun,

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:21.280
This is no time for your cozy relationship, Nonomura-kun.

00:13:22.270 --> 00:13:24.040
Bring it, Kageyama-kun!

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:24.870
Yeah!

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:30.950
I'm fired up.

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:32.160
As am I.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.030
Okay, let's go.

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:39.580
Ready... Go!

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.460
Gotcha!

00:13:45.420 --> 00:13:47.510
No control

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.340
Torako-san...

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:55.350
In the face, so she's safe.

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:57.280
How exactly is she safe?!

00:13:57.280 --> 00:13:58.470
How cruel...

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:00.070
I was making a call!

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:01.480
No, she's out, like out-out.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:03.600
Aren't you the smart-ass?

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:05.400
Nonomura, take a rest over there.

00:14:05.400 --> 00:14:06.920
That was just uncalled for.

00:14:06.920 --> 00:14:08.820
Sorry, Ayu...

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.540
Hey, Sengoku, give us a hand here!

00:14:13.400 --> 00:14:14.240
Me, too!

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.330
Yanagi, take care of her.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:17.090
And you?

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:18.960
I'll go get a towel from the locker room.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.890
Here, lean on my shoulder.

00:14:20.890 --> 00:14:23.790
I can walk, it's okay...

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:30.860
Here, have a wet towel.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:34.310
Put this on your head and lie down.

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:36.930
Thank you very much.

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.340
Okay, time to get this game started again!

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.650
Game, restart!

00:14:43.090 --> 00:14:45.440
Anyway, it's our ball, right?

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:53.200
Thanks to your safe pass, we can go on the attack!

00:14:57.860 --> 00:15:01.150
This isn't exactly how I anticipated things to go.

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:02.580
Torako-chan, watch out!

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:06.510
Take this!

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:13.020
Yikes!

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.300
Chie-chi!

00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:18.590
In the face:  Safe.

00:15:18.590 --> 00:15:20.090
Also, take her out of the game!

00:15:20.090 --> 00:15:21.690
Righto!

00:15:23.470 --> 00:15:24.610
My bad.

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.210
How dare you do that to Chie!

00:15:29.210 --> 00:15:31.370
Isn't it half your fault, Tora-chan?

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:34.640
She... She was a good person!

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:36.820
She had a dream, damn it!

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:42.710
A grand dream to build the best robots in all Japan with her own two hands!

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.020
This battle is to honor Chie's memory!

00:15:45.020 --> 00:15:47.170
But I'm not dead.

00:15:47.170 --> 00:15:50.130
Continue the match!

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:53.900
Hey, now!

00:16:02.030 --> 00:16:03.780
Tatsuki, get back!

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.960
Suzume-san, ah...

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:11.860
Suzume-san, Suzume-san...

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:17.360
Safe in the face, but she's out.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:19.030
Righto.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:25.000
Dummy!  You didn't have to hit her in the face!

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:27.430
This is just ghastly...

00:16:29.130 --> 00:16:30.990
Sengoku, we've got another.

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:31.690
Right!

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:33.010
Gotcha!

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.970
They're not moving.  It's almost like corpses lined up.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.720
We're not dead.

00:16:41.720 --> 00:16:42.640
They live again!

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:46.550
What the heck?  It's really is a death match.

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.570
Look at her, she's shaking in fear!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:51.570
Leftover Rice

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:55.030
We're the only survivors?

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:56.030
Leftover Bread

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:58.020
We don't have too many left, do we?

00:16:58.020 --> 00:16:59.240
Yeah.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.800
I didn't know dodgeball was such a dangerous sport!

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:07.210
And without Suzu on our team, we're screwed!

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:10.150
Hey, what're you doing?  Still gonna play?

00:17:10.150 --> 00:17:11.440
Kazamatsuri-kun!

00:17:11.440 --> 00:17:12.170
Touma!

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.920
Is it time for lunch yet?

00:17:14.920 --> 00:17:16.680
Not a chance

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:20.830
What's with everyone?

00:17:24.990 --> 00:17:26.180
A final round?

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:30.280
Yes!  At this rate we'll just get more people hurt,

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:34.170
so how about each team choose a representative and have them battle it out?

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:35.690
We should have done that from the start.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:39.890
Excellent!

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:43.210
Of course, our champion will be Saotome-kun.

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:44.750
And you?

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:53.380
We choose the homeroom teacher of our class 1-6, Amagasa Kyouichiro-sensei!

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:56.180
I refuse!  You trying to kill me!

00:17:56.180 --> 00:17:57.340
Please, Sensei!

00:17:57.700 --> 00:17:59.470
I won't slack off in class anymore, promise!

00:17:59.470 --> 00:18:01.780
You're the only one I can turn to!

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:03.290
God damn you!

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:04.980
I don't wanna die!

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:06.570
Neither do I!

00:18:06.570 --> 00:18:10.580
And anyway, there's some even better people to rely on than me over there, so...

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:12.900
Isn't that right, Sengoku?

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:14.680
What did you say?

00:18:15.210 --> 00:18:17.730
Me, fight in place of her?

00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:22.380
If she sees my brave figure stand up unflinching in the face of that murderous ball that has taken countless lives,

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:25.100
she would finally acknowledge my existence this time!

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.950
That's no good!  This is a problem for our class!

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:30.790
That's not the problem at all!

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.430
What's with those brats faces?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:39.310
It's like they're thinking "this guy's toast!"

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.390
Damn it to hell!

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.240
Bring it, Saotome!

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:55.100
I'll take you on!

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:57.820
Self Study

00:19:00.030 --> 00:19:03.260
Hey, Hitsugi, what have you been doing?

00:19:03.260 --> 00:19:06.680
What?  I've been studying.

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:07.890
It's self study, after all.

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:10.460
What have you been doing, Yagi-chan?

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:12.860
What?  Origami.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:13.920
It's free-time, after all.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:17.600
But this is really amazing.

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:18.760
How do you fold this?

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:21.050
That's the Statue of Liberty.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.960
Since it's "free-time" after all.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:28.490
Amazing.  But it's not free-time, it's self-study time.

00:19:28.490 --> 00:19:31.520
Same diff, Hitsugi.

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.740
So we didn't end up sketching anything.

00:19:38.740 --> 00:19:40.430
Let's just do it after school.

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:46.900
Yo.

00:19:59.710 --> 00:20:05.110
Torako's class was doing self-study over in the gym, see...

00:20:05.110 --> 00:20:08.220
I ended up watching it.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:11.870
Oh yeah?

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:13.980
That's it?

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:18.730
Take class seriously, Kitsune.

00:20:25.390 --> 00:20:28.320
Okay, that's all for today!

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:29.710
Stand.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:38.650
I feel like the pain is coming back.

00:20:38.650 --> 00:20:40.460
I said I'm sorry, jeez!

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:42.390
It's all sports' fault.

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:43.920
I'm sorry, really I am!

00:20:47.490 --> 00:20:48.760
Why you...

00:20:49.190 --> 00:20:53.600
Well, I suppose we ended up getting off easy.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:59.330
Amagasa-sensei, thank you so much for today!

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:00.770
No pwobwem.

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.780
How'ths hwuuthi-hwan?

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.650
I brought her with me!

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:05.730
Yuuki-chan!

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:18.450
Don't worry Sensei, you were really cool!

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:19.920
Justh shadthap, hwou hidiouth!

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:22.440
I said you were cool!

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:25.130
You managed to take Suzu's throws and not get knocked out!

00:21:25.130 --> 00:21:26.100
Shtop fawowing me!

00:21:26.100 --> 00:21:28.080
Suzu's throws are really amazing.

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:30.540
She can throw a shotput an amazing distance.

00:21:30.540 --> 00:21:33.100
Oh, if she had used a shotput today, you'd be dead!

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:34.670
Aren't you lucky, Sensei?

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:36.310
Wucky?  Yeah wight!

00:21:36.760 --> 00:21:39.230
Wucky?  Is that like your nickname or something?

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:41.340
Yeah, sho justh shadthap awweady!

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:43.110
Get well soon!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:45.630
I'm neba pwayin width you agwain!

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.220
Don't say that, come on...

00:21:48.220 --> 00:21:49.990
Nebah agwain!

00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:23.210
What's on Hyakko next week?

00:23:23.210 --> 00:23:25.080
It's a two-parter: "First a Daughter, Second a Son, and Third a Tiger Cub<i>"</i>

00:23:25.320 --> 00:23:27.960
and "A Demon's Heart for the Lost Tiger Cub<i>."</i>

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:30.630
Light will shine on the hidden past of Torako's big sister!

00:23:30.630 --> 00:23:31.230
Oh yeah?

00:23:31.230 --> 00:23:32.410
I just wanted to try saying that.

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:33.780
Look forward to next time!
